meta {
  name: Link Category to Product
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_ID/categories
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "id": "REPLACE_WITH_CATEGORY_ID"
  }
}

docs {
  `POST /api/v3/products/{product_id}/categories` — link one existing product
  category to a product. Confirmed live 2026-10-08 against "David's Dev Account"
  on a disposable product (`WC-REV-1008-A`), since deleted.

  ## Why this file exists: `category_ids` no longer works
  Until 2026-10-01 the documented way to attach a category was the
  `category_ids` array on `POST /products` or `PATCH /products/{id}`. **As of
  2026-10-08 that field is rejected on both verbs** with
  `422 {"errors":[{"name":"InputDTOValidationError","description":"category_ids:
  Extra inputs are not permitted"}]}`, even though `ProductCreateDto` and
  `ProductUpdateInputDto` in `openapi_pimv3.json` still declare it. The same
  applies to `static_list_ids`, `channel_ids`, `ecatalog_ids` and
  `product_data_sheet_ids` (quirk #93).

  This endpoint is the replacement. It implements the "1:M link a new entity
  instance" row that `materials/api-references/API V3 - status map (08_10_2026).md`
  marks **Direct** (pp. 11-13).

  ## Request shape
  The body is an object with a single `id` key naming the category to link —
  **not** a bare array and **not** `{"category_ids": [...]}`. Both of those are
  rejected:
  - `["<id>"]` → `422 "Input should be a valid dictionary or object to extract
    fields from"`
  - `{"category_ids": ["<id>"]}` → `422 "id: Field required"` plus
    `"category_ids: Extra inputs are not permitted"`

  ## Responses
  - **201** — `{"data": {"id": "<category_id>"}, "errors": []}`. Echoes the linked
    category's id, not the product.
  - **409 AlreadyExists** — the category is already linked. The message is
    unusually specific for this API and names both sides:
    `"'<category_id>' is already linked to products <product_id> through 'categories'"`.

  Link one category per request; there is no batch form.

  ## Related
  - Unlink: `Unlink Category from Product.bru` (`DELETE .../categories/{category_id}`)
  - Verify: `GET /products/{id}/categories` works again as of 2026-10-08
    (quirk #80's always-empty regression is resolved).
  - Assets do **not** support this pattern — `POST /products/{id}/assets` returns
    `405` (quirk #96).
}

example {
  name: Link Category - 201 Created
  description: Real response captured 2026-10-08 against "David's Dev Account", linking "WC Test Category" to disposable product WC-REV-1008-A.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6ac7ef509c6194f8c08e24aa/categories
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "id": "6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {"data": {"id": "6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc"}, "errors": []}
      '''
      }
      }
      }
      example {
      name: Link Category - 409 Already Linked
      description: Real response captured 2026-10-08, re-sending the identical link request from the 201 example above.
      request: {
      url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6ac7ef509c6194f8c08e24aa/categories
      method: post
      mode: json
      headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
      }
      body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
      {
      "id": "6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 409
      text: Conflict
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {"data": [], "errors": [{"name": "AlreadyExists", "description": "'6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc' is already linked to products 6ac7ef509c6194f8c08e24aa through 'categories'"}]}
      '''
      }
      }
      }
      example {
      name: Link Category - 422 Wrong Body Shape
      description: Real response captured 2026-10-08, sending the old {"category_ids": [...]} shape instead of {"id": "..."}.
      request: {
      url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6ac7ef509c6194f8c08e24aa/categories
      method: post
      mode: json
      headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
      }
      body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
      {
      "category_ids": ["6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc"]
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 422
      text: Unprocessable Entity
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {"data": [], "errors": [{"name": "InputDTOValidationError", "description": "id: Field required"}, {"name": "InputDTOValidationError", "description": "category_ids: Extra inputs are not permitted"}]}
      '''
    }
  }
}
